source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: root
---
Local-first API workbench for the terminal

Usage: rustman [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  init         Create a new workspace (rustman.toml, a local environment and a sample request)
  env          Inspect environments
  secret       Manage secret values (stored in the OS keychain, never in workspace files)
  cookies      Manage the cookie jars kept per environment
  auth         Log in to OAuth2-protected APIs
  import       Import collections (Postman, Insomnia, Bruno, HAR, .http, OpenAPI) and curl commands
  export       Export requests and collections (curl, code snippets, Postman, .http)
  explore      Explore an API from its OpenAPI document under the safety policy
  report       Print the report schema, render reports in other formats, diff them
  send         Send one request (a file, id or name, or an ad-hoc METHOD URL) and print the response
  run          Run the requests under files or folders and report the results
  bench        Load test request files and collections against one target origin
  stress       Find where a target listed in rustman.toml [stress] breaks, how, and whether it recovers
  graphql      Introspect GraphQL schemas and send GraphQL operations
  grpc         List and describe gRPC services, call methods and check health
  rpc          Send JSON-RPC calls and batches, and fetch OpenRPC catalogs
  history      List, inspect, replay and clear past exchanges (redacted)
  mcp          Serve the workspace to AI agents over MCP (Model Context Protocol)
  mcp-client   Explore and call MCP servers: their tools, resources and prompts
  completions  Print a shell completion script: rustman completions zsh > _rustman
  tui          Open the terminal UI (the default when stdin and stdout are a terminal)
  webhook      Capture, inspect and mock inbound webhooks on a local listener
  snapshot     List snapshot files and prune the ones no request uses
  mock         Serve an OpenAPI document as a local mock server
  ws           Open WebSocket sessions: send frames and print received messages
  sse          Listen to Server-Sent Events streams and print their events
  contract     Contract testing: classify OpenAPI changes as breaking or not, Pact contracts and passive conformance
  trace        Open the trace link of a past exchange in the browser
  viz          Open a run or exploration report in the graphical viz companion (rustman-viz)
  docs         Generate static API documentation from the workspace, or preview it
  monitor      Scheduled monitors: run collections on a schedule, store the results locally and alert
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
